er b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335082#post1335082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you can make a moral choice between a genocidal wolf-born beast born to kill in the name of nature and a sociopath murderous undead manipulator, generalizing on all the garou race, well, I'm happy for you.<br /> I can't <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those sociopath is good in solving unwanted pregnancies problem))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T07:13:09-07:00","id":1335109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335087#post1335087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those sociopath is good in solving unwanted pregnancies problem))</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the avarage red talon can say the same about himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T10:34:10-07:00","id":1335150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335076#post1335076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VtM characters wasn't mean to be a good guys. And they don't call themselves a heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone in VtM thinks they're the heroes of the story.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla thinks they're the heroes because their structure and rules keep vampires and humans as safe as possible. They're the line between humans hunting vampires to extinction, and vampires becoming mad tyrants ruling over humanity as night-kings. Of course, the Cam is also an oppressive institution that asserts itself on you if you like it or not (esp. it's right to kill you because of its rules), that spends more of its resources enriching the few and exploiting the many.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs think they're the heroes because they can do everything the Cam does, without being a bunch of power hungry elitist assholes about it. They're deluded to think that they're anything more than repeating the same mistakes as the Cam though, because there is a level of organization and institution you need to really balance the Masquerade and vampire nature against each other. You can't just have everyone off doing things their own way.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat think they're the heroes because they're not deluding vampires about the reality of the WoD. Th ancient blood gods can awaken at any moment and wipe out humanity and vampires, so all the petty squabbling about control and human morality and what not is dooming everyone that doesn't get on board with just accepting that vampires and monsters, but the worst of the worst need to be fought not turned into myths and forgotten. And of course, they're the most morally atrocious group of the bunch.<br /> <br /> You seem to be struggling with the difference between &quot;protagonist&quot; and &quot;good guy.&quot; The WoD games generally focus on protagonists, not good guys, as the player characters; even if they're not the worst guys to help keep them good protagonist material.<br /> <br /> The Garou aren't meant to be good guys, even if to 90s sensibilities the were more sympathetic than the vampires as being on the right side of human social issues more than not. What they call themselves is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335080#post1335080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I really don't like the imbalance between &quot;Garou are heroes who you suppose to rooting for&quot; and &quot;Garou are stupid angry motherfuckers and hypocrites&quot;. I know, that's kinda the point but it never worked well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine. WtA isn't your game. Cool. Tastes differ. Don't try to make it more than what it is.<br /> <br /> If you don't wan to play the contradiction between the good heroic ideals of the Garou against their hypocrisy and failures, WtA isn't the game for you. That doesn't make it a bad game, or a game you need to misrepresent to others to justify your tastes. It's no different than someone that doesn't like the juxtaposition of vampires as creatures of deep personal horror, and vampires as political monsters in an epic shadow war. <br /> <br /> You can try to cut out the parts of the game you don't like. You can muddle through if you're having fun anyway. You can go play something else.<br /> <br /> Stirring up needless antagonism between fans doesn't solve your problem, or help anyone else,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T16:49:29-07:00","id":1335213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335031#post1335031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou kill vampires whenever they can. OIf their position would be like &quot; Don't touch us and go away&quot; I would would be the first who'd approved them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Humans kill Vampires whenever they can. Vampires kill vampires whenever they can. The default possition of being a vampire is &quot;SHIT WANTS TO KILL ME FOR BEING A MONSTER&quot;. Notice how ever &quot;moral&quot; vampire group... is particularly prone to murdering kindred.<br /> <br /> Garou are not special in hating and killing vampires. They are just the ones Vampire stupidly poke their fingers in and get killed the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T16:55:35-07:00","id":1335216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335059#post1335059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You guys are not slightly better than - average - camarilla vampire. When a Garou kills a vampire with Humanity 7 - who most probably hurt well less people than this garou himself - that's just plain wrong.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Humanity 7 isn't &quot;The average&quot; its a neonate untouched by the real issues. 4 and 5 are &quot;average&quot; humanities for vampires who've actually done something. This is before the fact that Kindred society by its nature is a vast conspiracy to hide all sorts of criminal acts and thus while Humanity 7 vampire may not have done something personally evil by being a part of a vast conspiracy to protect various slavers, murders and so on who will NEVER be punished for it. They have intrinsically made the world worse. There's a reason why all the &quot;Good&quot; splats in Vampire intrinsically wish to murder other Vampires.<br /> <br /> You'll notice how the EVEN at best the justification for this is &quot;if humans knew about us they would kill us all&quot; so vampires work from the premise that they are such monsters they cannot be known about. That Humans would just kill them on sight there is no reasoning with people. Garou are litterally treated no differently than NORMAL PEOPLE. Except you know.. normal people can't tear you in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T21:48:05-07:00","id":1335250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335216#post1335216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Humanity 7 isn't &amp;quot;The average&amp;quot; its a neonate untouched by the real issues. 4 and 5 are &amp;quot;average&amp;quot; humanities for vampires who've actually done something. This is before the fact that Kindred society by its nature is a vast conspiracy to hide all sorts of criminal acts and thus while Humanity 7 vampire may not have done something personally evil by being a part of a vast conspiracy to protect various slavers, murders and so on who will NEVER be punished for it. They have intrinsically made the world worse. There's a reason why all the &amp;quot;Good&amp;quot; splats in Vampire intrinsically wish to murder other Vampires.<br /> <br /> You'll notice how the EVEN at best the justification for this is &amp;quot;if humans knew about us they would kill us all&amp;quot; so vampires work from the premise that they are such monsters they cannot be known about. That Humans would just kill them on sight there is no reasoning with people. Garou are litterally treated no differently than NORMAL PEOPLE. Except you know.. normal people can't tear you in half.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou treated differently than mages and fairies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T22:29:28-07:00","id":1335256,"title":"","content":"No, they're not.<br /> <br /> Multiple posters have all explained repeatedly that the Garou anti-vampire bias isn't actually special for the WoD.<br /> <br /> If you're here to convince people? You're failing because you're refusing to engage with what people are saying. You're never going to convince people by directly contradicting the books to make your point.<br /> <br /> If you're here to receive some sort of ego-boost for you insight? You're not going to get it, because you're not saying anything useful, insightful, or meaningful to people that actually know these games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T23:51:56-07:00","id":1335264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335256#post1335256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're not.<br /> <br /> Multiple posters have all explained repeatedly that the Garou anti-vampire bias isn't actually special for the WoD.<br /> <br /> If you're here to convince people? You're failing because you're refusing to engage with what people are saying. You're never going to convince people by directly contradicting the books to make your point.<br /> <br /> If you're here to receive some sort of ego-boost for you insight? You're not going to get it, because you're not saying anything useful, insightful, or meaningful to people that actually know these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK well. You're right. Garou are not gonna change couse of my disappointment. Tbh, I stopped to bother about oWoD because of Garou but... Old habits die hard)<br /> I just thought... what if OnyxWolf changed this only thing a bit. So I could love WtA again)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 09-12-2019, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T02:42:40-07:00","id":1335287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335064#post1335064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metagame: couse VtM is a separate splat (the main one for oWoD) while Fomori and Infernalists are antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you read a vampire game core book, Lupines are antagonstits. If you read WtA, vampires are. As are Hunters. Tha game lines aren't meant to be mixed. The PCs of one game are supposed to be NPCs in the other.<br /> <br /> Besides that, vampire PCs are bullshit. They have to sleep the whole day. Their entire (un)life cycle is a ridiculous burden to everyone, most of all the ST who would have to adapt all planning to night time plots.<br /> Just for your information: Here in Germany people sleep at night. There is for example, by law, no 24/7 bodega (maybe a gas station shop, in rare cases).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335064#post1335064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inuniverse: Werewolves should actually hunt those vampires who are on the way. But not adequate and normal Anarchy and Camarillian.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not recognise a vampire if the vampire doesn't do something that is worth killing it for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335080#post1335080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I really don't like the imbalance between &quot;Garou are heroes who you suppose to rooting for&quot; and &quot;Garou are stupid angry motherfuckers and hypocrites&quot;. I know, that's kinda the point but it never worked well for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, it didn't work for you. <br /> Personally I see it as a contradiction that makes a facaded character, not unlike the vampire monster who pretends to be a part of society, adhering to the social standards and convention of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335264#post1335264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK well. You're right. Garou are not gonna change couse of my disappointment. Tbh, I stopped to bother about oWoD because of Garou but... Old habits die hard)<br /> I just thought... what if OnyxWolf changed this only thing a bit. So I could love WtA again)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you let someone talk you out of lovin' WtA in the first place?<br /> <br /> I mean, from a WtA standpoint there is nothing bad in killing vamps and from a VtM standpoint there is nothing bad about Lupines in the woods trying to kill vampires.<br /> <br /> The only problem about one splat &quot;inherently hating&quot; another would arise when you attempt crossover. And if you are frustrated because you can't be a vampire accepting, yet traditional garou in a troupe of vamps. So, be an exception. A changeling supplement made a garou the camarilla prince of a small town, yeahy crossover. If a group of traditional garou doesn't want a vampire amongst them, well so don't play one. Maybe convince them of a mummy, risen, lich or - urgh - thinblood, or don't play with them.<br /> <br /> Accepting each game as it's own standalone game, with interlinking elements, is the solution to the dilema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T07:32:29-07:00","id":1335309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335250#post1335250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou treated differently than mages and fairies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No they don't Garou aren't even practically treated as differently from NORMAL PEOPLE. Generally speaking the two things that will get a vampire killed by a Garou: Invading their territory(something that I will repeatedly point out any and every other supernatural type is just as guilty of killing vampires for ESPECIALLY other vampires) and B the Vampire does something horrifically monsterous infront of said Garou, like eat a baby or kill a family or frenzy and eat someone(its like the Masquerade serves a purpose or something)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T12:52:52-07:00","id":1335336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335264#post1335264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought... what if OnyxWolf changed this only thing a bit. So I could love WtA again)</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need Onyx Path or White Wolf (they are and never have been the same company) to change anything.<br /> <br /> The only thing that needs to happen is for you to let go of whatever misrepresentations convinced you that what you want wasn't always the case in the actual game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T16:42:39-07:00","id":1335372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1335264#post1335264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK well. You're right. Garou are not gonna change couse of my disappointment. Tbh, I stopped to bother about oWoD because of Garou but... Old habits die hard)<br /> I just thought... what if OnyxWolf changed this only thing a bit. So I could love WtA again)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope Scourges are still a thing! Vampires regularly kill high humanity &quot;Wouldn't hurt a fly&quot; types because they are too thin of blood. The natural reaction to an elaborate criminal conspiracy of vampires was... the government trying to take them out(and being rather far more successful than any garou has ever been!)<br /> <br /> The Anarch movement and Camarilla are at eachother's throats So its probably worse than ever for vampire survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T18:08:40-07:00","id":1335380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1334896#post1334896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a lot less common than it was 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> IME, back when there was just the WoD, the tension between fans of the games was much higher and the OP's concerns could have been more meaningful to me. Call it a silver lining or whatever, but the original end of the WoD, and the start of the (now) CofD, heralded a fairly large unification of WoD fans (esp. as this time period was also a major shift in popular game design, and small press distribution).</div> </div> </div> </div>I sometimes wonder if I was some sort of strange outlier just because I tended to enjoy all of the games equally back then, though usually for different reasons. I think from around 95 or so going forward, the idea was that while they share the same general setting, they were all meant to be separate stand alone games. <br /> I also remember when Hunter: The Reckoning first came out, and alt.games.white-wolf was full of &quot;Hunters are RACIST<sup>1</sup> because they hunt my favorite character type!&quot; I think there's always been a class of World of Darkness fan who wants their Gangrel, Garou, Verbena and Changelings to all dance together in moonlit glades to the music of Loreena McKennitt (or whatever the current equivalent is), and if you like that sort of thing, cool, but you're never really going to see that take in any source material that came out after 1995. <br /> <br /> (In my own games, I tend to treat the entire planet as much more xenophobic in general than the real world, as its a part of the Gothic genre and it's a natural outgrowth of living in a world full of inhuman forces that constantly seek to prey on people. Any stranger is a potential threat, and that belief persists among urban ethnic enclaves, the LGBT+ community, religious minorities, upscale gated communities, small towns, tribal peoples, and so forth all over the globe. Likewise among the supernatural, where all of them are under constant threat from some outside force - vampires from discovery by the living and from the plots of their own kind, Garou from the forces of the Wyrm and Weaver, mages from the Technocracy, wraiths from the forces of Oblivion, and changelings from Banality and other enemies. As they say, it's not paranoia if someone is actually out to get you.)<br /> <br /> <sup>1</sup>And I really get annoyed when people casually throw terms like that or &quot;fascist&quot; around as lazy synonyms for &quot;something I don't like.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T06:43:09-08:00","id":1357040,"title":"","content":"Also, do you know who are -kinda- seems to be more descent persons than Garou? Bloody Mummers from ASOIAF. While complete fuckheads, they at least are Equal Opportunity Villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T07:57:00-08:00","id":1357050,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRIQKq-AncwQ2h0gQi3-EfbxasoeM35x0BlNHIMkAztGXZLmbLnPw&amp;s\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> That being said...<br /> <br /> I have to say that I fail to see why <i>being partial with vampires</i> (of all things) it's so villainous.<br /> <br /> I mean, most vampires are like a fusion between the worst of the Lannisters and the White Walkers. And those who are not, are still dangerous monsters at one bad day from killing everyone in their vecinity *all* the time.<br /> <br /> Generalizing, Garou aren't nice people. They're monsters, brutes and fanatics...<br /> <br /> ...but of all the things they did in their long history (and still do), killing vampires ain't THAT bad in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-26-2019, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T10:01:26-08:00","id":1357066,"title":"","content":"Oh God... IT LIVES!!!<br /> <br /> IT LIVES IGOR! IT LIVES! IT LIVES! IT LIIIIVVVESSSS!!!!!<br /> <br /> *clears throught*<br /> <br /> Frankensteinian hysterics aside, let's get back into this I guess. Why not. Gives us bored forum users something to do while everyone sleeps off the holidays.<br /> <br /> Alright so first of all, comparing the Bloody Mummers, a ASOIAF mercenary company with horrific methods and arguably one of the basest portrayals of humanity in all of ASOIAF (which is saying something), to the entirety of the Garou Nation is rather loaded and I'd say that a few similarities aside, the better comparison for the BM would almost certainly be the Black Spiral Dancers.<br /> <br /> That aside, yes vampires do exist on a spectrum. Young vampires are often no less humane then anyone else. Some even stay relatively humane as they age. Yet, noteworthy exceptions to this rule aside, vampires become inhuman as they age. That's the whole narrative point of Vampire: the loss of humanity and the struggle involved.<br /> <br /> The reason they tend to become inhumsne though is fairly obvious. They literally hunger for human blood. They have a supernatural compulsion to rip and tear and glut themselves constantly. Their nature is to be possessive, greedy, and obsessive. They are the worst elements of humanity and each one struggles to resist those instincts that come from both The Beast and their basest nature peeled away from illusions and laid bare.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that vampires are all horrible people or unsympathetic, but from a human viewpoint they are unconditionally horrific an monstrous. They just are.<br /> <br /> Now, the garou, particularly the Garou Nation as a political entity, is also horrific and monstrous. The setting itself makes numerous fair arguments positing the villainy of the Nation. Even at their most heroic, taken all together, the GN is darkly anti-heroic at best. That's part of what makes it so interesting. It's a dark people using dark methods to fight an inarguably necessary fight.<br /> <br /> If you wanna discuss the inhumanity of the Garou Nation I've got plenty of ideas. Their history of genocide and attempted genocide. Their treatment of metis. Their treatment of kinfolk (at times; some are better then others yes but the point stands). Their willingness to kill innocent people to preserve their veil of secrecy. Their unapologetic loathing of human civilization despite its numerous virtues. Their callous refusal to acknowledge the misery that would befall humanity if they succeeded in many of their ultimate goals.<br /> <br /> The Garou are not unsympathetic, yet they have many horrific and terrifying aspects of their culture, that's what makes them interesting enough to be the spearhead of an entire major setting and game line of books.<br /> <br /> Yet, of all the things to use to paint them as unambiguously nefarious, as Aleph said, their relationship with vampires seems perhaps the most bizarre.<br /> <br /> Because frankly the average garou is rarely more heroic and useful to humanity as when they are tearing apart the average gang of vampires with teeth, claws, and holy wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T14:10:43-08:00","id":1357103,"title":"","content":"Complaining about werewolves frequently hunting and killing vampires seems even weirder when the relationship between vampire and werewolf was first set up in Vampire. And one of the sample characters from The Hunter's Hunted was a werewolf gunning for vampires to avenge the death of his mate, again, some time before W:tA existed. This whole thread has just been one long &quot;Who Killed Hannibal?&quot; bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T04:44:10-08:00","id":1357182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357066#post1357066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna discuss the inhumanity of the Garou Nation I've got plenty of ideas. Their history of genocide and attempted genocide. Their treatment of metis. Their treatment of kinfolk (at times; some are better then others yes but the point stands). Their willingness to kill innocent people to preserve their veil of secrecy. Their unapologetic loathing of human civilization despite its numerous virtues. Their callous refusal to acknowledge the misery that would befall humanity if they succeeded in many of their ultimate goals.</div> </div> </div> </div> All of it is more or less ok for such are dark setting. From the metagame POV, though, the loathe towards ALL the vampires seems kinda too much hypocritical. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T05:10:46-08:00","id":1357184,"title":"","content":"Wow.... necroed and we're right back to the the fully debunked nonsense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T05:26:55-08:00","id":1357186,"title":"","content":"Well somehow Changelings don't think that vampires must be killed without question, despite the high Banality. Neither ALL the mages hate ALL the vampires (Hermetists hate Tremere, while Akashi and Choral are not represents mages asawhole)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 12-27-2019, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T05:56:58-08:00","id":1357190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow.... necroed and we're right back to the the fully debunked nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now we're back to the whole: &quot;but others (that have a different social structure, goals, and generally represent none of the core *themes* of WtA) don't hate vampires in exactly the same way&quot;<br /> <br /> It IS truly astounding...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T06:21:30-08:00","id":1357191,"title":"","content":"I think Kindred and Garou might support the same causes (like the Toreador and the Silver Fangs of House Winter Snow both backing the Jacobite Rebellion from Outlander), but they are unlikely to ever directly work together. Vampires support the growth of cities, while werewolves fight to preserve the wilderness. Their ultimate goals are directly in conflict. Do you guys agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T07:39:06-08:00","id":1357198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357191#post1357191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Kindred and Garou might support the same causes (like the Toreador and the Silver Fangs of House Winter Snow both backing the Jacobite Rebellion from Outlander), but they are unlikely to ever directly work together. Vampires support the growth of cities, while werewolves fight to preserve the wilderness. Their ultimate goals are directly in conflict. Do you guys agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish their relations were like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T07:49:47-08:00","id":1357199,"title":"","content":"I agree to some extent. The problems werewolves have with vampires go further than &quot;wilderness vs. cities&quot;, but they can certainly have the same goals on a small, more concrete, scale.<br /> <br /> BSD are enemies of both, Vampires are enemies of both (that is, &quot;other vampires&quot; are enemies of <i>both</i>, if you get what I mean), and surely there can be other coincidences (Gangrel protecting the same forest against the same Pentex subsidiary, albeit for unrelated reasons it's a classic) <hr /><br /> Garou, as a Nation have vampires as both &quot;public enemy&quot; and unholly abominations. But the more &quot;micro&quot; one gets, the more nuances to this enemity one can find. As has been said in the thread previously, to say that Garou reaction to vampires it's &quot;kill on sigth&quot; it's an oversimplification. Most of the time Garou have other things on their plate, and leave vampires be.<br /> Also, as I stated previously, Garou are no hive mind (albeit they ARE a close knit tribal society). Clans don't hate all with equal strength, nor have all Garou the same <i>approaches </i>to such universal enemity. There's various hues of black to that universal loathing, so to speak, and individual Garou may subvert expectations even more based on their personal experiences or reasons (very rare in such a closed culture, but not unheard of).<br /> <br /> From a metagaming POV, while the &quot;Garou vs the world in general and vampires in particular&quot; it's a staple of the game that's very dear to it's fans, crossover stories with Garou among other splats aren't going away because there's also a lot of people who like to do that. Older editions toyed with the idea of vampires with A Garou ally, Garou with A vampire ally, pacts of non-agression, etc. And &quot;The enemy of my enemy&quot; it's a staple of ALL WoD.<br /> <br /> The setting leaves <i>less </i>room to wriggle a Garou into &quot;the party&quot; on a crossover game compared with vampires or mages (that are much more individualistic creatures, and thus more free to act outside the norm or believe whatever they want), but there are places to find exeptions to the general rule. There's plenty of Merits and written lore to make it happen, if one wants it to happen.<br /> <br /> And that's where this thread comes so baffling to me. It isn't clear to me if the complains are about Garou <i>morality</i> as part of the setting, or about the game design making crossover hard (in which case it's nonsense to say Garou &quot;are too villanous and hipocrite&quot;. There's no ethical pressure here, it's just a choice of &quot;game design&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-27-2019, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T11:31:40-08:00","id":1357224,"title":"","content":"I'll try to throw out some points to further the discussion, but in large parts I agree with exactly what Aleph just said. The setting exists on a spectrum when one considers specific scenarios and opportunity is laid for stories of either style or leaning, especially when you add the Golden Rule into the mix.<br /> <br /> Anyway though, I'll hop back up to where I left off yesterday.<br /> <br /> \u2022Loathing All Vampires Is Hypocritical:<br /> -Sure, maybe. It's not so much hypocritical in the sense that they say one thing and do another large scale about their vampiric policy, but I can see the argument that the Garou have no right to be the moral judges of anything. Sure. Fair enough. Yet due to their nature, they need to serve that role. If they stop, the world ends. As far as the Garou are concerned, they are fighting an eternal battle against Stagnation and Corruption incarnate and every wasted moment further's their causes. The vast majority of vampires, to some degree, are indirectly serving these concepts and are probably feeding into them more then the average bane or pattern spider and definitely more so then the average person. The garou's animosity towards kindred is very much grounded in their core motivations, which despite all the atrocity the Garou have caused, their ultimate goals and ideals are undeniably noble.<br /> <br /> \u2022Changelings &amp; Mages<br /> -Yeah, not all changelings and mages are trying to actively murder vampires. Hell, they may even work with kindred if it benefits them. But that's a false equivalency. The goals of the Fae &amp; Mages are, by and large, radically departed from those of the Garou Nation. The Garou are literally divinely appointed spiritual warriors. This task is their duty, not that of some random mage or fae.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, while you're certainly right that mages (and to a lesser extent) fae are capable of working with vampires, outside of Nephandi, Thalliain, and the truly corrupt; I sincerely doubt that you'd be able to find many who know of vampires who wouldn't agree that humanity as a whole would be better off if they were wiped from the face of the earth. Individuals may be fine, but as a breed vampires are a parasite and a cancer.<br /> <br /> The more motivated sorts of factions such as House Scathach and the Order of Hermes have said this since forever. The main reason why other supernaturals don't seek to destroy vampires in is pure pragmatism generally, not any particular sympathy towards this nocturnal breed of monster.<br /> <br /> \u2022Working Together<br /> -Yet what we've discussed here is largely the rule and every rule has exceptions. Like Vancouver's Compact in canon, truces are a common conceit where mutual benefit or some other local circumstance can necessitate it and those can certainly be interesting. Plenty of material posits examples of such alliances and they are genuinely interesting.<br /> <br /> Yet in the case of Vampires-Werewolves specifically it's important to note that for even the tribes most likely to go for it, Glass Walkers or Bone Gnawers, it's generally a case of ends justifying the means and frying bigger fish. Any truce with leeches in the eyes of the Garou is temporary. They've been betrayed too many times to rest easy and they have a saved duty. Whether now or centuries from now, vampires too must be eradicated to complete their holy service to Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T12:16:17-08:00","id":1357229,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T14:32:41-08:00","id":1357254,"title":"","content":"I will mention that one of the reasons the various Outcast factions - Caitiff and thinbloods; Ronin, lost cubs, and Skinwalkers; Orphans and Hollow Ones (sort of) - exist is so that the people who want to do a mixed group can do so without most of the sociopolitical baggage getting in the way. But it's not really meant to be the default position for any of the gamelines' main protagonists, all of whom are justifiably paranoid and largely certain of their own superiority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-27T18:39:39-08:00","id":1357280,"title":"","content":"Vampires are objectively of the Wyrm, so Garou have a religious obligation to oppose them. In addition to this, the Garou oppose vampires for all the same reasons ordinary humans do - vampires view everyone else as prey. Not only do Garou need to worry about themselves in this regard, they have more reason to fear for their kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Having said that, Garou - just like humanity - have their shirkers, their criminals, and their ambitious who will make deals with the devil to get what they want. So we can expect that there is a not insignificant number of Garou who interact with vampires on an ongoing basis, There was more prevalent in earlier editions which portrayed various Garou, even prominent ones, of having various motivations and dedication to the Litany. In Revised, the setting was increasingly portrayed in heroic fantasy lights, and these kinds of Garou either weren't mentioned anymore or were outright killed.<br /> <br /> Of course, there is differences between the tribes on their frequency of interaction with vampires.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers had the most interaction, with various books stating outright the tribe had allies among Nosferatu and the Sabbat. The tribe overall did not really follow the Litany anymore, and half of its &quot;members&quot; were essentially AWOL. The typical refrain of &quot;Garou wouldn't do that&quot; just didn't apply to that tribe. Bone Gnawer run septs would likely to be viewed by other tribes as corrupt hellholes. (again, this was heavily changed in Revised in a deliberate attempt to make them more heroic).<br /> <br /> The Glass Walkers, by virtue of living in the cities, also had to make accommodation with vampires. If they didn't, they'd have to be at war constantly with them. While perhaps not formal treaties, they'd likely have informal agreements with the vampires in their city overall (vampires know they should avoid Washington Park, while Glass Walkers know to keep out of certain night clubs, etc.) and specific agreements between individuals. Certainly, the larger the city, the more likely the vampires got the better end of the deal. Perhaps only in small cities - of a few hundred thousand population - which had a caern that attracted one or more dozen Garou, would the Glass Walkers attempt to outright destroy any vampires and make it a hostile environment. But once the human population was large enough to support a significant number of vampires, especially relative to the # of Garou there, anything other than sporadic violence would be more likely to be their disadvantage. Glass Walkers would be much more likely than the Bone Gnawers to avoid the appearance of scandal - they are trying to position themselves as the next leaders of the Garou, needed in the urban future. So such deals would be kept hush hush and out of sight. But there's likely to be many ongoing deals which the tribe doesn't look down on - provided people keep them discrete.<br /> <br /> Then you have the political tribes that publicly denounce any interactions with vampires, and privately police it as well, yet have various individual members, packs, and camps which do make deals with them for various reasons and motives. Shadow Lords fit this most of all, but Uktena, Children of Gaia, and even Silver Fangs have more than a few such members. Shadow Lords are more likely to do it as part of their intrigues. Uktena in order to gain occult knowledge. Children of Gaia in order to &quot;redeem&quot; high humanity vampire or because of naive views of love. And Silver Fangs as a distasteful necessity. But here above all the rule is &quot;don't get caught,&quot; because there will be no mercy if you do. But if discovered by friends and allies, they have a chance it will either not be mentioned, or they will stage a private intervention rather than be exposed immediately.<br /> <br /> The other tribes are much less likely to interact with them, but very small numbers of individuals still do for the exact same reasons as above. But any discovery of their acts will probably result in immediate trial and punishment. There would simply be less understanding of the &quot;need&quot; to make compromises.<br /> <br /> And of course, ronin and Lost Cubs exist outside Garou society and would do whatever they wanted.<br /> <br /> One thing I do object to is the use of the term &quot;racism&quot; to describe Garou (or indeed anyone's) dislike for vampires. It is a totally inappropriate term. It is like saying humans dislike of the smallpox virus is because of racism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T00:42:13-08:00","id":1357320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357190#post1357190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And now we're back to the whole: &quot;but others (that have a different social structure, goals, and generally represent none of the core *themes* of WtA) don't hate vampires in exactly the same way&quot;<br /> <br /> It IS truly astounding...</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing vampires is not the primal goal of Garou, neither it nessesary for them. That's just the thing that made Garou even more unsympathetic. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T05:26:38-08:00","id":1357345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357320#post1357320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing vampires is not the primal goal of Garou, neither it nessesary for them. That's just the thing that made Garou even more unsympathetic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is part of their primary goal, as ALL creatures of the Wyrm are to be destroyed. It just isn't AS personal as with BSDs or banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T11:21:41-08:00","id":1357378,"title":"","content":"To your last point Lashet, what Ana Mizuki said.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but I take from your choice to call out that alone that you at least acknowledge the arguments that Aleph, No One of Consequence, Black Fox, others and I have been making.<br /> <br /> You don't have to like that it's the case and you don't have to run your table in accordance with them, but if you're discussing canon and setting default, this is how it is.<br /> <br /> Also, as an aside, I feel that while 'racism' definitely deserves more attention as an inappropriately used term here, the 'xenophobia' of the thread title is another. The Garou Nation definitely has a cultural trend of xenophobia, which would be an interesting topic of discussion, but this is not that and that thus makes the title of the thread misleading. <br /> <br /> Something akin to 'Garou-Vampire Prejudice' or 'Garou-Vampire Relations' may have served better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-28T13:05:24-08:00","id":1357389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357378#post1357378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To your last point Lashet, what Ana Mizuki said.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, but I take from your choice to call out that alone that you at least acknowledge the arguments that Aleph, No One of Consequence, Black Fox, others and I have been making.<br /> <br /> You don't have to like that it's the case and you don't have to run your table in accordance with them, but if you're discussing canon and setting default, this is how it is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How I see it/understand from the books, it is more like an exterminator killing off mice as opposed to rats. There is no personal beef, but it is their job. Sure, there are two tribes that legit DO hate vampires, but then it is more that they hate specific clans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T00:08:37-08:00","id":1357474,"title":"","content":"Also, speaking of thermes. <br /> I remember my argues with Garou-hatrrs from those times I was WtA -fun. Their point - Garou would kill a sentinent beings (vampires) for formal reason (just for being vampires) which is close to racism and nazim. According to current consensus in fandoms, there is nothing worse than fashism and to be a fashist is complete crossing of Moral Event Horizon, hence your average Garou is worse than Ramsey Snow (although Ramsey is a rapist, which is also taboo, so your average Garou is more like equal to Ramsey). <br /> Sorry, if usingsuch terms was offensive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T02:40:00-08:00","id":1357490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357474#post1357474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, speaking of thermes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing in your post has anything to do with themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their point - Garou would kill a sentinent beings (vampires) for formal reason (just for being vampires) which is close to racism and nazim. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't.<br /> <br /> There is nothing uniquely racist or Nazi about declare something a crime punishable by death; even for actions that aren't directly the crime of the one being punished (like getting Embraced). It's something that's been part of human law since, literally, we started writing laws down. Thousands of years before the rise of the modern concept of racism or the Nazis.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't a race in the sense racism means. You can't be racist against all of something. If you think all humans are inherently evil, you're not a racist, you're a misanthrope. If you think all vampires are evil, you're whatever the equivalent of a misanthrope would be towards vampires.<br /> <br /> The Garou belief that vampires are inherently of the Wyrm and thus must be destroyed is religious fanaticism, not the scapegoating of minorities the Nazi's used to justify their atrocities.<br /> <br /> Of course people also toss around the word &quot;sentient&quot; like it's some special qualifier. Sentient just means &quot;feeling.&quot; Every farm animal, from dairy cows, to horses used for work, to guard dogs, to chickens bred for slaughter, to a barn cat? Those are all sentient beings, as they're all capable of the emotional capacity for feelings that sentient means. Every bane, fomori, and BSD a Garou kills for being what it is, was also sentient.<br /> <br /> Sapient is the word that humans actually care about (we're called <i>Homo sapiens</i> for a reason), but also something entirely ill-defined. It's an ephemeral idea of wisdom that separates use from other animals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to current consensus in fandoms... </div> </div> </div>You really don't have the grounds to be speaking of any sort of consensus on this.<br /> <br /> Also... you don't seem to get what fascism is either. Fascism doesn't apply to this. It's a governing philosophy. Killing people because Gaia said to isn't fascism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...hence your average Garou is worse than Ramsey Snow (although Ramsey is a rapist, which is also taboo, so your average Garou is more like equal to Ramsey). </div> </div> </div>This doesn't follow the rest, and makes no sense. Ramsay wasn't a fascist, he was part of a feudal system and never claimed any inclination towards a different mode of government. The power afforded to feudal lords was plenty to sate his sadistic urges.<br /> <br /> Your average Garou isn't doing something because they enjoy causing pain and suffering, which was Ramsay's primary emotional motivation. Hence, this claim is another load of bunk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sorry, if usingsuch terms was offensive </div> </div> </div>If you're sorry, why did you use them? And worse, use them in such an offensively wrong way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-29T06:00:38-08:00","id":1357516,"title":"","content":"One important thing I think this thread has overlooked. <br /> Vampires are social master wizards. You engage with dialogue with one, chances are it'll bewitch you. You'll be his best friend for an hour and divulge important secrets or you'll get back to the sept and find yourself on a killing spree. Not only are they excellent manipulators but vampires have social magic, man, you can't just try to reason with one, because they'll always win. You will be compromised, and your pack will have to act accordingly or suffer the consequences. Naturally, this fear of being compromised makes Shoot First Never Ask Questions the only reasonable option. <br /> <br /> Oh, yeah, you argued that vampires are better than humans because they're not using plastic bottles and such. <br /> The impact of individuals on the planet is nothing compared to corporations. Vampires have a big influence with the latter. They have a vested interest in increasing urbanization so that they have more options for food, in increasing corruption and the gap between rich and poor to better their feeding opportunities whilst minimising the risks. You can even get into very esoteric actions like increasing the height of buildings and gaining thicker smog so that the sun becomes a lesser threat. Every bright eyed neonate left to live will some day become a cynical ancilae and then an elder, who will perpetuate this urban corruption. <br /> <br /> Garou are literally powered by rage and a removal from reality, they're flawed. They're also brought up in isolated communes and indoctrinated into a theology and ideology that promotes obedience and punishes subversion. They're taught the world is sick and they're the god-given cure... But given most of the values they're taught they've got more in common with libertarian miliitias or christian cults than Nazis. Sure, they've got imagined pasts, but they have to defend great defenseless earth-mother figure from big-bad father evil. Many of the pleasing fictions are very left-wing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T10:19:24-08:00","id":1357820,"title":"","content":"I wish I could like your last post more then once Heavy Arms. It's a succinct and accurate reply which deconstructs the opposing argument very well and in a very satisfying way, imo. There's nothing I could add on top of that so I just want to say: thank you, that was awesome.<br /> <br /> Along with what MyWifeIsScary (May Gaia grant I never meet her then : D) said, its stated numerous times that the Garou have been tricked, betrayed, and brought to ruin for trusting vampires, not even working with them or making formal alliances-just trusting them, for MILLENIA. The Garou Nation has a history of tragedy and betrayal attached to vampires that dates back to the First City (especially if you agree with the theory that Ennoia, progenitoress of the Gangrel clan, was kinfolk) and to this very day. Given everything we knew about garou as an honor martial culture with a strong oral tradition, all kenning garou would be aware of numerous tales of this genre. Also, given that Garou are of the nature to murder each other and other fera, their abject allies, over grudges that can be centuries or millennia old, the fact that we have as few garou as we do roaring into places like New York City, Chicago, &amp; Mexico City to commit mass killings and property destruction is frank a miracle and a sign of just how desperate the focused war effort against the Wyrm is for modern garou.<br /> <br /> Another big agreement with MWIS, and not just because twisting the environment argument to target the actions of individuals instead of corporations is how I gain Rage irl. Vampires, as a whole, are compared to parasites and cancer for a reasons and it's not entirely rhetoric. A vampire is a cancer just smart enough to not be caught and not kill it's host while still weakening from them and destroying them from within for as long as possible. Young vampires hunt and have small gatherings of blood dolls. Older vampires have turned themselves into the top of a bloody feudal empire that constantly draws fresh blood up to them, siphoning off of humanity perpetually. Vampires lobby to keep slums poor and the impoverished in poverty, because it gives them poorly lit places to send their minions to abduct people that no ones will miss and where the police are bought for cheaper then next's months rent. That's on the small scale too. That's just what your local ancillae or young elder does to get by. Conspiracies of elders and ancients lobby nation states and push things in their favor and what's in their favor is rarely ever good for humanity at large. With only their own self-decided limits and the rivalry of their peers holding them in place, as they help make the World of Darkness as shadowy as it is, vampires form great corporations of corruption that corrude humanity and drain it of its life, without ever offering it the dignity of a fair fight or the peace of an eventual demise.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation is flawed, I don't think many here would argue that. It's horribly flawed and in many interesting ways. It holds some of the worst aspects of Neolithic and early human social structure alongside its benefits and provides an interesting contrast to the modern world which they fight. The Garou Nation, as a political entity, is a militant xenophobic theocratic terrorist state.<br /> <br /> Yet despite that, this conversation has actually done more to convince me of the heroism of the Garou's campaign of slaughter against vampirism then anything I've ever experienced in game or from the rhetoric of any garou in a White Wolf title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:00:39-08:00","id":1357848,"title":"","content":"My Malkavian PC had dots in Herd. The ST asked me, &quot;Oh, yeah, what's the story with that?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Oh, he's made the psychiatric hospital his own personal feeding ground. When his fuel tank is running low, he Obfuscates inside, puts on a white coat, and goes around taking 'blood samples.' Nobody believes the patients' 'wild stories'.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, yeah, it wouldn't surprise me if a werewolf wanted to kill him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T14:15:31-08:00","id":1357883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1357224#post1357224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022Working Together<br /> -Yet what we've discussed here is largely the rule and every rule has exceptions. Like Vancouver's Compact in canon...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it's cannon. But the compact was violated by the vampires and the sept destroyed, it's members killed. Check the Glass Walker Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T14:57:45-08:00","id":1358260,"title":"","content":"I don't see why Garou get such a bad wrap about killing vampires. its a drop in the bucket compared to how many are killed by the Camarilla for being &quot;thin blooded&quot; or &quot;not acknowledged&quot; or &quot;a shovel head&quot; or &quot;because I'm the Prince&quot; etc. Most Kindred are killed by other Kindred. This is OCCASIONALLY overcome by poor masquerade practices by Mundanish humans(Non imbued hunters).<br /> <br /> At no point are Werewolves any more on the problem for your average Kindred than your average Surfer is going to get attacked by sharks. Yes it happens. Its scary and its over reported. As long as you aren't swimming in shark area generally nothing happens. But Humans are the REAL danger that's why MASQUERADE is the central conceit of the game line. The central conceit of Vampire is such complete fear that humans will murder them in their sleep that they need to make humans not believe they exist. This is not something they do with Garou. They don't try to remove all memories of Vampires existing from Garou. They don't go hunting Garou who &quot;know too much&quot; they don't even put them on their damned Redlist.<br /> <br /> The natural innate human state of reaction to Kindred is to destroy them, garou are just scarier. Garou are not unique in their vampire hatred. Vampire hatred is the natural state of beings. All of Vampire society is built around elaborate rules to control the impulse to kill eachother. Treating Garou as having a unique reaction when rather its the standard reaction is silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-01-2020, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T10:57:47-08:00","id":1358449,"title":"","content":"I like most of what you said there, but I do believe that, upon finding out about vampires, a person with any power will ask 'what's in it for me?' and a person without power will get squashed the moment they try to do anything. If you're afraid by your discovery, you'll know that blowing the horn will get you killed faster than not. Garou are in a position where they're not afraid of the lone vampire who intrudes on their territory, as individually they're usually much more powerful and'll usually be able to bring at least a packmate, but garou are entirely afraid of starting an actual war with the vampires; they'd certainly lose through attrition. They could near-wipe a city in a day with planning, but the retaliation's not something they could bear. Unless a vampire is very seriously courting the Wyrm they're not going to go on the offensive in a large city (perhaps a smaller one)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T20:37:28-08:00","id":1358532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1334774-garou-and-xenophobia?p=1358449#post1358449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like most of what you said there, but I do believe that, upon finding out about vampires, a person with any power will ask 'what's in it for me?' and a person without power will get squashed the moment they try to do anything. If you're afraid by your discovery, you'll know that blowing the horn will get you killed faster than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes a single piece of wood in the middle of the day to kill even the most potent of elders especially post withering. But even before the most recent situations Kindred society has been defined since the dawn of time by hiding from the Kine. As powerful as kindred think they are they have profound weaknesses that allow them to be readily taken down and they know it.<br /> <br /> This is before the fact some Kindred sees a hunter going through and thinning the ranks and thinks &quot;Hey I can use this to free up this territory over there&quot;. That is the natural state of Kindred to be predator and prey at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou are in a position where they're not afraid of the lone vampire who intrudes on their territory, as individually they're usually much more powerful and'll usually be able to bring at least a packmate, but garou are entirely afraid of starting an actual war with the vampires; they'd certainly lose through attrition. They could near-wipe a city in a day with planning, but the retaliation's not something they could bear. Unless a vampire is very seriously courting the Wyrm they're not going to go on the offensive in a large city (perhaps a smaller one) </div> </div> </div>Garou have shit to do. For all their Wyrminess Kindred are fairly low on priorities sake. That's before being pretty good at not sticking out by working through humans. Most &quot;Garou kindred interactions&quot; probably gets to &quot;kindred pokes his influence at Garou problems.. loses some pawns decides to work on something else because he can always get more mortals&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And those who don't fall under either of the categories above are neonates who are even worse off. All the weaknesses of having to sleep during the day and none of the decades of build up to deal with it. I think there's a statistic that most kindred don't last 5 years in one of the books that should say something about their situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}